  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening and scaling up HIV and TB prevention response in Panama - Panama (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Panama, TB/HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Panama)This program has the following goals: HIV Prevention for key populations.  Integrated HIV care for key populations.  Reduce TB mortality in Panama.  Reduce the burden of TB in Panama.  Reduce the HIV/TB burden in Panama.  Strengthen the national HIV/AIDS response. The objectives of this program are: Improve ARV treatment adherence levels.  Improve the social environment towards the elimination of stigma and discrimination in people living with HIV and key populations.  Increase TB screening among HIV patients.  Increase the capture of TB suspects.  Increase the detection of MDR-TB at national level.  Provide opportune diagnosis y adequate follow-up to key populations.  Reduce TB treatment lost to follow-up among identified key populations.  Reduce the HIV transmission rate in key populations</narrative>
  </description>
